# Session-Based Testing First: Test-Driven Development

## Purpose
Enforce strict test-driven development within each session where Supertest E2E tests are written before implementation, tests drive design decisions, and all tests must pass before session completion.

## Session TDD Core Principle

RED → GREEN → REFACTOR (per session)

1. RED: Write test that fails (at session start)
2. GREEN: Implement minimum code to pass test (during session)
3. REFACTOR: Improve code while keeping tests green (before session end)

## Session Testing Context

Each session follows TDD principles:
- Session N: Write E2E tests for current endpoint
- Session N: Implement endpoint to make tests pass
- Session N: Refactor while keeping tests green
- Session N: Document test results in session summary

## E2E Testing Patterns

### Test Structure
Every endpoint test follows this structure:

```typescript
import request from 'supertest';
import app from '../../src/app';

describe('POST /api/resources', () => {
  it('creates a resource on the success case', async () => {
    // Arrange: Setup test data
    // Act: Make request
    // Assert: Verify response
  });

  it('returns an error for invalid input', async () => {
    // ...
  });

  it('validates required fields', async () => {
    // ...
  });

  it('requires authentication', async () => {
    // ...
  });
});
```

### Using Skeleton Mock Data
Phase 0 skeleton provides expected output structure.

**Step 1: Capture mock response**
```
# From Phase 0 skeleton
POST /resources returns:
{
    "resourceId": "mock-123",
    "name": "Mock Resource",
    "description": "Mock description",
    "ownerId": "mock-owner",
    "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}
```

**Step 2: Write test using structure**
```typescript
it('creates a resource with real implementation', async () => {
  const response = await request(app)
    .post('/api/resources')
    .set('Authorization', `Bearer ${testToken}`)
    .send({
      name: 'Test Resource',
      description: 'Test description',
      ownerId: 'test-owner-123',
    });

  // Verify structure matches skeleton
  expect(response.status).toBe(201);
  const data = response.body;

  // Check all fields present
  expect(data).toHaveProperty('resourceId');
  expect(data).toHaveProperty('name');
  expect(data).toHaveProperty('description');
  expect(data).toHaveProperty('ownerId');
  expect(data).toHaveProperty('createdAt');

  // Verify data correctness
  expect(data.name).toBe('Test Resource');
  expect(data.description).toBe('Test description');

  // Verify dynamic fields
  expect(data.resourceId).not.toBe('mock-123'); // Should be a real ID
  expect(data.createdAt).not.toBe('2024-01-01T00:00:00Z'); // Should be an actual timestamp
});
```

### Test Fixtures
Create reusable test fixtures in `tests/setup.ts`:

```typescript
// tests/setup.ts
import { randomUUID } from 'crypto';
import request from 'supertest';
import app from '../src/app';

export async function createTestUser(): Promise<{ email: string; token: string }> {
  const email = `test-${randomUUID()}@example.com`;
  const response = await request(app)
    .post('/api/auth/register')
    .send({ email, password: 'testpass123', fullName: 'Test User' });
  return { email, token: response.body.accessToken };
}

export async function getAuthHeaders(): Promise<{ Authorization: string }> {
  const { token } = await createTestUser();
  return { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` };
}

export function buildTestResource(overrides: Partial<Record<string, unknown>> = {}) {
  return {
    name: 'Test Resource',
    description: 'Test description',
    ownerId: 'test-owner',
    ...overrides,
  };
}
```

### Testing Patterns by HTTP Method

**POST Endpoints:**
```typescript
it('creates a resource', async () => {
  const headers = await getAuthHeaders();
  const response = await request(app)
    .post('/api/resources')
    .set(headers)
    .send({ name: 'New Resource', description: 'Description' });

  expect(response.status).toBe(201);
  expect(response.body.resourceId).toBeDefined();
  expect(response.body.name).toBe('New Resource');
});

it('rejects invalid input', async () => {
  const headers = await getAuthHeaders();
  const response = await request(app)
    .post('/api/resources')
    .set(headers)
    .send({ name: '' }); // Invalid: empty name

  expect(response.status).toBe(400);
});

it('requires authentication', async () => {
  const response = await request(app)
    .post('/api/resources')
    .send({ name: 'Resource' });

  expect(response.status).toBe(401);
});
```

**GET Endpoints:**
```typescript
it('retrieves a resource by id', async () => {
  const headers = await getAuthHeaders();
  const created = await request(app).post('/api/resources').set(headers).send(buildTestResource());
  const resourceId = created.body.resourceId;

  const response = await request(app).get(`/api/resources/${resourceId}`).set(headers);

  expect(response.status).toBe(200);
  expect(response.body.resourceId).toBe(resourceId);
});

it('returns 404 for a nonexistent resource', async () => {
  const headers = await getAuthHeaders();
  const response = await request(app).get('/api/resources/nonexistent').set(headers);
  expect(response.status).toBe(404);
});
```

**PUT/PATCH Endpoints:**
```typescript
it('updates a resource', async () => {
  const headers = await getAuthHeaders();
  const created = await request(app).post('/api/resources').set(headers).send(buildTestResource());
  const resourceId = created.body.resourceId;

  const response = await request(app)
    .put(`/api/resources/${resourceId}`)
    .set(headers)
    .send({ name: 'Updated Name' });

  expect(response.status).toBe(200);
  expect(response.body.name).toBe('Updated Name');
});
```

**DELETE Endpoints:**
```typescript
it('deletes a resource', async () => {
  const headers = await getAuthHeaders();
  const created = await request(app).post('/api/resources').set(headers).send(buildTestResource());
  const resourceId = created.body.resourceId;

  const response = await request(app).delete(`/api/resources/${resourceId}`).set(headers);
  expect(response.status).toBe(204);

  const getResponse = await request(app).get(`/api/resources/${resourceId}`).set(headers);
  expect(getResponse.status).toBe(404);
});
```

## Unit Testing Patterns

Unit tests are written AFTER E2E tests pass.

### Service Layer Tests
Mock the Prisma-backed repository to test business logic in isolation:

```typescript
// tests/services/resource.service.test.ts
import { ResourceService } from '../../src/services/resource.service';
import { ResourceRepository } from '../../src/repositories/resource.repository';

jest.mock('../../src/repositories/resource.repository');

describe('ResourceService', () => {
  let mockRepo: jest.Mocked<ResourceRepository>;
  let service: ResourceService;

  beforeEach(() => {
    mockRepo = new ResourceRepository(null as never) as jest.Mocked<ResourceRepository>;
    service = new ResourceService(mockRepo);
  });

  it('creates a resource successfully', async () => {
    const input = { name: 'Test', description: 'Description', ownerId: 'owner-123' };
    const expected = { resourceId: 'resource-123', ...input, createdAt: '...', updatedAt: '...' };
    mockRepo.create = jest.fn().mockResolvedValue(expected);

    const result = await service.createResource(input);

    expect(result.resourceId).toBe('resource-123');
    expect(mockRepo.create).toHaveBeenCalledWith(input);
  });

  it('propagates repository errors', async () => {
    mockRepo.create = jest.fn().mockRejectedValue(new Error('Database error'));

    await expect(
      service.createResource({ name: 'Test', description: 'Description', ownerId: 'owner-123' })
    ).rejects.toThrow('Database error');
  });
});
```

## Test Organization

```
tests/
├── routes/                 # E2E tests for API endpoints (Supertest)
│   ├── health.test.ts
│   ├── auth.test.ts
│   └── resources.test.ts
├── services/                # Unit tests for business logic
│   └── resource.service.test.ts
└── setup.ts                 # Shared fixtures / app factory
```

## Session Test Execution Strategy

### Session Development (TDD Cycle)
```bash
# Run specific test file while implementing in current session
npx jest tests/routes/resources.test.ts

# Watch mode
npx jest --watch tests/routes/resources.test.ts
```

### Session Completion
```bash
# Run all E2E tests for current session
npx jest tests/routes/resources.test.ts

# Run all tests to ensure no regressions
npx jest

# Run with coverage for session
npx jest --coverage
```

## Test Data Management

### Database State
For E2E tests using a real database:
- Use unique identifiers (`crypto.randomUUID()`) to avoid conflicts
- Wrap each test in a Prisma `$transaction` and roll back, or truncate tables in `beforeEach`
- Prefer a dedicated test database (`DATABASE_URL` override in `.env.test`) over sharing dev data

### Mock Data Consistency
Use consistent patterns:
```typescript
// Test IDs
const TEST_USER_ID = 'test-user-123';
const TEST_RESOURCE_ID = 'test-resource-456';
const TEST_ITEM_ID = 'test-item-789';

// Test timestamps
const TEST_TIMESTAMP = '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z';
```

## Assertions Best Practices

### Be Specific
```typescript
// Good: Specific assertions
expect(data.name).toBe('Expected Name');
expect(data.resourceId).toBeDefined();
expect(typeof data.createdAt).toBe('string');

// Bad: Too generic
expect(data).toBeTruthy();
expect('name' in data).toBe(true);
```

### Test Error Messages
```typescript
// Good: Verify error details
expect(response.status).toBe(400);
expect(response.body.detail).toBe('Invalid resource ID format');

// Bad: Only check status code
expect(response.status).toBe(400);
```

### Test Side Effects
```typescript
// Good: Verify state changes
const response = await request(app).post('/api/resources').set(headers).send(resourceData);
expect(response.status).toBe(201);

// Verify resource was actually created
const getResponse = await request(app).get(`/api/resources/${response.body.resourceId}`).set(headers);
expect(getResponse.status).toBe(200);
```

## Session Testing Checklist

Before completing any session:

- [ ] Session plan reviewed and test objectives confirmed
- [ ] E2E test written before implementation
- [ ] Test initially fails (proves it tests something)
- [ ] Test uses skeleton mock data structure
- [ ] All success cases tested for current endpoint
- [ ] All error cases tested for current endpoint
- [ ] Authentication tested
- [ ] Zod validation tested
- [ ] All E2E tests passing for current endpoint
- [ ] Unit tests added for complex business logic
- [ ] Test coverage adequate for new code
- [ ] Tests are maintainable and readable
- [ ] Session summary documents test results

## Session Testing Anti-Patterns

Do NOT:
- Skip session plan review
- Write implementation before test
- Skip test because "it's simple"
- Test implementation details instead of behavior
- Use arbitrary `setTimeout`/sleeps instead of proper async/await
- Share state between tests
- Forget to test error cases
- Test only happy path
- Commit code with failing tests
- Skip tests during "rapid development"
- Test endpoints from other sessions
- Skip session test documentation
